{"title":"1977 AHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_25\">Problem 25</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 25\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the largest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83cd5ce806e74e37da7ebb96ab110045990f6a0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1005!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02bedd46306390e4c9b9293a00c7de6620b71b9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/274021bbf42f02799ddfc0290909e17a07173f74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }102\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }112\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }249\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }502\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\text{none of the above}\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"581\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We first observe that since there will be more 2s than 5s in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83cd5ce806e74e37da7ebb96ab110045990f6a0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1005!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />, we are looking for the largest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83cd5ce806e74e37da7ebb96ab110045990f6a0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1005!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />. We will use the fact that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/2/1a2a9ae5f0cac44d75db08321a83d87e4f9c2fb3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = \\left \\lfloor {\\frac{1005}{5^1}}\\right \\rfloor + \\left \\lfloor {\\frac{1005}{5^2}}\\right \\rfloor + \\left \\lfloor {\\frac{1005}{5^3}}\\right \\rfloor \\cdots\\]\" width=\"285\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>(This is an application of Legendre's formula).\n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5bb215d21ddfbe2ec17a99cb7118ca80e4a2ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=5$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and onwards, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa1c35a41d011772302987f3d138777ca78c0caf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lfloor {\\frac{1005}{5^k}}\\right \\rfloor = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"96\" height=\"45\" />. Thus, our calculation becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff8b8686c28898646e7044ccd6e98f295c65ad65.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = \\left \\lfloor {\\frac{1005}{5^1}}\\right \\rfloor + \\left \\lfloor {\\frac{1005}{5^2}}\\right \\rfloor + \\left \\lfloor {\\frac{1005}{5^3}}\\right \\rfloor + \\left \\lfloor {\\frac{1005}{5^4}}\\right \\rfloor\\]\" width=\"341\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/232c9785272533dbe8b5b6fc35c26afafdd3d43c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = \\left \\lfloor {\\frac{1005}{5}}\\right \\rfloor + \\left \\lfloor {\\frac{1005}{25}}\\right \\rfloor + \\left \\lfloor {\\frac{1005}{125}}\\right \\rfloor + \\left \\lfloor {\\frac{1005}{625}}\\right \\rfloor\\]\" width=\"341\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd7bacd3c39d6174a9258ae0b4c9e44aee53e2d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = 201 + 40 + 8 + 1 = \\boxed{250}\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>Since none of the answer choices equal 250, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfc0829f3f29bbf35d0a861644e00cfef0f50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>- mako17\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016220729\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 58/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3257/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17373:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016220729 and revision id 166731. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}